Today on Hidden Brain the subtle biases that cause very smart and very skilled people to become their own worst enemies and how innovators have found a way to help pilots, doctors, frankly any of us perform at our best. It's a story of an ancient insight applied to modern life, and even though you might not know it, this innovation shapes life and death decisions that affect all of us. We began in the depths of the Great Depression. It was a time of great suffering and people were looking for inspiration.
今天在 Hidden Brain 节目中：导致非常聪明和极其能干的人成为自己最大敌人的微妙偏见，以及创新者如何找到方法帮助飞行员、医生——坦率地说，帮助我们所有人——发挥出最佳水平。这是一个将古老见解应用于现代生活的故事，尽管你可能并不知情，但这种创新正在塑造着影响我们所有人生死抉择。我们要从大萧条的深渊说起。那是一个苦难深重的时代，人们在寻找精神鼓舞。

