00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:57.000
You know, kids would obsess over who was leading the rankings at the Cleveland Air Races. The military was obsessed with the idea of long-range bombers, planes that could better protect the U.S. coastline and give the nation an edge if another great war erupted. In 1934, the Army Air Corps put out a proposal to the nation's aviation companies and challenged them to build a new, long-range bomber for the military. The prototypes were to go up against each other at a flight competition the following year. The two leading competitors are Douglas and Boeing.
你知道的，孩子们会痴迷于谁在克利夫兰飞行大赛的排名中领先。军方则痴迷于远程轰炸机这一概念——这种飞机能够更好地保护美国海岸线，并在爆发另一场大战时赋予国家优势。1934年，陆军航空兵向全国的航空企业发出招标，向它们发起挑战，要求为军方建造一款新的远程轰炸机。原型机将在次年的飞行比赛中一决高下。主要的两个竞争对手是道格拉斯和波音。

