00:06:39.000 --> 00:07:08.000
The morning of the competition, flight teams from Boeing, Douglas and Martin, assembled with military leaders at Wright Field in Dayton, Ohio. Early in the morning, with 9 o'clock in the morning, and apparently by all accounts, a very beautiful day, so kind of ideal conditions for a late October day in Ohio, and perfect day for a test flight, really. A crowd watched as the Boeing 299 taxi to the runway. Advances, the power, engine spool up, is rolling down the runway.
比赛当天的早晨，来自波音、道格拉斯和马丁公司的飞行团队与军方领导人一起聚集在俄亥俄州代顿的莱特机场。大清早，早上九点钟，从各方面来看显然是个非常晴朗的日子——对于俄亥俄州十月下旬的一天来说，条件可以说是理想之选，而且确实是进行试飞的完美一天。人群注视着波音 299 滑向跑道。推进，动力，引擎转速提升，它正在跑道上滑行。

13
00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:31.000
The beautiful airplane lifted into the air. It had all the makings of a winner. And then the observers noted that the aircraft starts to abruptly pitch up. So as it takes off, rather than gradually rising and building up speed, the nose just rising and building up speed, the nose just starts to pick up and up and immediately observers on the ground realize something is wrong.
这架美丽的飞机升空了。它具备了一架获胜飞机的所有要素。随后，观察员们注意到这架飞机开始突兀地仰头向上。因此，在它起飞时，并没有逐渐爬升并积蓄速度，而是机头径直开始向上抬起并加速，机头刚开始向上抬起，地面上的观察员立刻意识到情况不对劲。

14
00:07:31.000 --> 00:08:02.000
Very wrong. At 300 feet, the aircraft stalled. As people watched in horror, the flying fortress began to plummet toward the Earth. It impacts the ground in a flat attitude and in person to flames. There were five crewmen on board. Major ployer Hill, who was the chief of flight tests for right field, Leslie Tower, who was the chief of flight test pilot. There was also Donald Tut, who was acting as the co-pilot.
大错特错。在 300 英尺的高空，飞机失速了。在人们惊恐的注视下，“空中堡垒”开始向地面坠落。它以平直的姿态撞击地面，瞬间陷入火海。机上当时有五名机组人员。担任莱特机场首席试飞员的少校普洛耶·希尔，以及担任首席试飞员的莱斯利·托尔。还有担任副驾驶的唐纳德·塔特。

15
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:34.000
There was a mechanic on board, Mark Cougler, and John Cutting, who was one of the aeronautical engineers involved with the program. Obsovers on the ground raised to what the wreck. Obviously an aircraft like this has a lot of fuel on board, and so when in this case, because the aircraft came down relatively flat, it only just started to spin in, it would have been fairly apparent to the people on the ground. There was a good chance of survivors. So it's kind of a worst case scenario where you see that the aircraft is involved in terms
机上还有一名机械师马克·库格勒，以及参与该项目的航空工程师之一约翰·卡廷。地面的观察员冲向残骸。很显然，像这样的一架飞机携带有大量燃油，因此在这种情况下，由于飞机是以相对平直的姿态坠落的，只是刚刚开始旋转着坠毁，对于地面上的人来说，这应该是相当明显的。有很大的生还可能。所以这算是一种最糟糕的情况，你看到飞机失事起火，但你知道上面的人可能还活着。因此，这对救援人员和机上人员来说都将是极大的危险。

16
00:08:34.000 --> 00:09:22.000
of being on fire, but you know there's people on there that are likely still alive. So it's going to be a great hazard to both the rescuers as well as the occupants of the aircraft. Three of those occupants survived, but two died, blow your hill and Leslie Tower. Both were highly experienced pilots. Almost immediately people asked, what made the flying fortress crash? This aircraft did have an autopilot and not unlike a lot of accidents today, attention centered on that. So was the autopilot somehow engaged where it was overriding the inputs of the crew members. So that was one focus of the investigation, but very quickly attention turned to a control locking mechanism, which was, that was one of the advanced features of this aircraft,
机上有三人生还，但有两人遇难：普洛耶·希尔和莱斯利·托尔。两人都是经验极其丰富的飞行员。人们几乎立刻问道：是什么导致了“空中堡垒”坠毁？这架飞机确实配备了自动驾驶仪，和今天的许多事故并无二致，人们的注意力集中在了这一点上。那么，是否是自动驾驶仪在某种程度上处于开启状态，从而覆盖了机组成员的手动操作？因此这是调查的重点之一，但很快人们的注意力就转向了一个操纵锁定机构，这是该飞机的先进功能之一，

17
00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:54.000
was that it had its own built-in mechanism for locking the elevator for when it was essentially parked on the ground. The elevator determines the pitch of the plane, basically the movement of the nose up or down. For most planes at the time, elevator locks were on the outside, meaning ground crew had to unlock them before take-off. But in the Model 299, the elevator lock was inside the cabin of the plane. The crew had forgotten to unlock it. And so after the plane took off, the pilots found they couldn't level off.
即它拥有内置机构，用于在飞机基本上停在地面上时锁住升降舵。升降舵决定了飞机的俯仰角，也就是机头向上或向下的运动。对于当时的大多数飞机来说，升降舵锁都在外部，这意味着地面人员必须在起飞前将其解锁。但在 299 型飞机上，升降舵锁在飞机座舱内部。机组人员忘记将其解锁了。因此飞机起飞后，飞行员发现他们无法保持水平飞行。

