00:11:35.000 --> 00:12:05.000
But Roger says that kind of thinking may not have saved the man who died in the crash. The pilots actually had lots of experience with the plane. They had been flying it for several months. Things had become rather routine in testing this aircraft. So certainly the crew, both at right field and with Boeing, were fairly familiar with it. They had clearly become quite comfortable with the operation of the aircraft and were used to its quirks and how it performed. So if more training was in the answer, what was?
但罗杰说，那种想法可能无法拯救在坠机中丧生的那个人。飞行员们实际上对这架飞机有着丰富的经验。他们已经驾驶它好几个月了。在测试这架飞机的过程中，事情已经变得相当常规化。因此，无论是莱特机场还是波音公司的机组人员，对它都相当熟悉。他们显然对飞机的操作变得非常适应，并习惯了它的脾气和性能。所以，如果更多的训练不是答案，那答案是什么？

